WEBVTT

NOTE Original complete video/audio are preserved.
Source speech alignment and confirmed corrections are recorded privately.

1
00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.800 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
Who is this so-called society?

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.680 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
They say you committed
a crime against society.

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.000 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
That's what it says on
the paper: against society.

4
00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:16.080 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
But stop for a moment with that word
in your hand. Ask a question almost no one

5
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.320 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
asks. Who is she?

6
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:23.500 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
Because no one rebels against a building.
No one feels anger at a written law.

7
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.140 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
No one breaks the window of something
that never looked at them.

8
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:34.120 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
So imagine society as a person.
An old woman. She's been here a long

9
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:40.080 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
time, longer than you, longer than
me. She has her customs. There's a

10
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:45.520 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
time and way for everything. She has
written rules, the laws, and other rules

11
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:51.260 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
no one wrote, yet everyone enforces.
She has values, beliefs, and what she

12
00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:57.060 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
calls right and what she calls
wrong. And she's not perfect. Far

13
00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:02.940 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
from it. She has children she
loves up close and others she keeps

14
00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:08.340 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
away. She has favorites, makes mistakes.
She's primitive in many ways, too.

15
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.760 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
You were born in her house. But there's
a part of that house you've never

16
00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:20.520 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
entered. There was a school that didn't
wait for you, a door to a job that didn't

17
00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.600 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
open. There were people who crossed
the street and didn't see you.

18
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:30.460 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
There was a place at the table that
was never yours. And here I need to

19
00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:33.460 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
tell you something very difficult.
She didn't throw you out.

20
00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:39.700 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
She just didn't look. No meeting,
no decision. No one gathered to choose

21
00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:44.840 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
you. She was distracted, caring for others
close by. She left the door closed

22
00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:47.060 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
without realizing there
were people outside.

23
00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:53.070 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
That doesn't undo what you felt. But it
changes one thing: it wasn't against you.

24
00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:59.050 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
It was neglect. And neglect hurts
almost as much as malice. Only

25
00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:04.930 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
no one to hate in the end. Then anger
came. I want you to notice something

26
00:02:04.930 --> 00:02:10.730 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
about anger, because almost no
one notices. Those who rebel still

27
00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:15.610 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
expect something. No one's angry with a
stranger, or shouts at someone who never

28
00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:21.450 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
owed them anything. Anger is the sound
of an experience, of a hope that fell

29
00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:26.530 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
to the ground and broke. So you struck
her house, broke the glass, took what was

30
00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:32.250 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
hers, or hurt someone she loves.
And it wasn't against an abstraction.

31
00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:38.390 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the end, it was us. Always us.
And she did what anyone does

32
00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:44.250 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
when they're hurt inside their own house.
She put you far away. She called that

33
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:50.150 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
a sentence. But inside, it was what it
always is: someone hurt, keeping away

34
00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.210 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
whoever hurt them.

35
00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:57.050 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
Now look where you both are. Two hurt
people. One outside, with a broken window,

36
00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:02.730 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
one in here, with a locked door.
Each waiting for a sign from the other.

37
00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.300 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
And waiting, yes, can
take a lifetime, right?

38
00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.460 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
Some people die waiting,

39
00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.580 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
right? They leave here, go back out,
still waiting for someone to come first.

40
00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.760 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
No one comes. So they come back here.

41
00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:20.780 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
So the question that decides your
life isn't who did more wrong.

42
00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:22.640 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
It's another question. This one:

43
00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.900 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
who takes the first step?
And I'll tell you,

44
00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.740 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
plainly: it has to be you.
Not because you did more wrong.

45
00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:37.040 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not because you deserve less, or she's
right and you're not. But because it's you

46
00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.600 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
holding that paper in your hand.
You're the one reading this now.

47
00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:47.200 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
She won't read it. She doesn't even know
we're here on Instagram. And your life

48
00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:52.060 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
is yours. While you wait for her
to change, she's the one controlling you.

49
00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:58.160 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
The day you move without
waiting, you regain control

50
00:03:58.160 --> 00:03:59.160 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
of yourself.

51
00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:03.060 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
Taking the first step, folks,
doesn't mean being weaker.

52
00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.140 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
It's being the only one there
who still wants to live.

53
00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:07.900 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
And that has a name:

54
00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:09.620 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
humility.

55
00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:14.800 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not the humility of bowing your
head. That's not it. It never was.

56
00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:20.500 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
Humility is to stop keeping score,
to stop adding up what she did to you,

57
00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:25.380 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
to stop remembering every closed
door, every sideways glance,

58
00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:31.520 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
every no. Let go of the ruler in your
hand. While you measure who owed

59
00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:35.940 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
more, you remain imprisoned.
And I'm not talking about jail.

60
00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:42.260 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
Reconciling isn't saying only you were
wrong. It means: I'll stop counting.

61
00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:48.000 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
I will build. Notice the word they
use for this: reintegration. Whole

62
00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:53.520 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
means complete. To integrate is to make
one again. And re- at the start means

63
00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:59.280 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
again. So you're not entering, you're
returning. Because the place was yours

64
00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:05.080 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
from the start. No one gifted it to you,
no one took it away. You just never

65
00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:07.680 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
reached it. And how do you return?

66
00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:13.780 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not with speeches. She doesn't hear
speeches. You return through work well

67
00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:18.880 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
done when no one's watching. Through
the word you keep. Through the honor you

68
00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:24.360 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
respect. By respecting the officer who
opens and closes your door each day.

69
00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:30.360 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
Through the fights you don't pick. Through
the hand you offer someone who arrived

70
00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:35.660 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
today and is afraid, as you once were.
That's how, quietly, with no one

71
00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:41.280 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
applauding. That old woman's suspicious,
with reason. She'll take a long time

72
00:05:41.280 --> 00:05:45.820 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
to believe in you. Let her take her time.
You're not doing this so she'll see it.

73
00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:51.940 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
You're doing it to become that. She's
still there, with her house, her rules,

74
00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:57.740 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
her flaws, her distrust. Imperfect like
you, like me, like everything that's

75
00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:02.140 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
alive. And there's still a place at
the table that's never been occupied.

76
00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:04.200 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
She doesn't know your name.

77
00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:08.070 line:90% position:50% align:center size:90%
But she still can.
